# MiniMax-M2.7 Q3_K_S for the PeerReviewer benchmark.
#
# THE BUG THIS FIXES
# ------------------
# The upstream quant ships two stop strings that do not belong to this
# architecture:  stop "<|im_end|>"  and  stop "</think>".
#
# MiniMax-M2 is not a ChatML model. Its role markers are ]~!b[ ]~b]system
# ]~b]user ]~b]ai ]~b]tool with [e~[ as the message end, and eos_token_id
# 200020 -- so "<|im_end|>" is never emitted and that stop is simply inert.
# It is the second one that breaks the model: M2.7 emits <think>...</think>
# and THEN the answer, so stopping on "</think>" ends generation at the exact
# moment reasoning finishes. Ollama routes reasoning into message.thinking,
# so the caller receives thinking=N chars, content=0 chars, done_reason=stop.
# Verified twice in ai_code_review.yml (runs with thinking=7033 and
# thinking=8837 chars, both content=0, both done_reason=stop at ~2k of the
# 40000 num_predict budget -- not a length problem).
#
# Redeclaring PARAMETER stop in a child Modelfile REPLACES the inherited list
# rather than appending to it (verified against a scratch model), so the single
# line below is enough to drop both bad stops. [e~[ is the model's real
# end-of-message marker; EOS 200020 terminates normally regardless.
#
# Do NOT add a custom TEMPLATE here. Overriding it with something like
# {{ .Prompt }} discards the ]~b]ai role framing the model was trained on, and
# because such a template never references {{ .System }} it silently drops any
# SYSTEM block too. The inherited template is correct -- leave it alone.
# TEMPLATE: leave it alone, and note it is not what you think.
# An earlier build clobbered this tag with TEMPLATE """{{ .Prompt }}""", which
# `ollama show --modelfile` still reports. That line is INERT for this model:
# Ollama uses a built-in renderer for the minimax-m2 architecture, and
# /api/show returns the real 6512-char Jinja template (]~b]ai, ]~b]user, [e~[,
# <minimax:tool_call>) regardless of the Modelfile TEMPLATE.
#
# Verified functionally against 192.168.10.100: an API system message saying
# "reply with exactly PINEAPPLE" was quoted back in the model's reasoning and
# obeyed. A {{ .Prompt }} template has no {{ .System }} reference and would
# have dropped it silently, so the built-in renderer is demonstrably in charge.
# The `thinking` and `tools` capabilities confirm it -- {{ .Prompt }} carries no
# think markers, so those can only come from the renderer.
#
# Consequence: do NOT re-import from the GGUF to "repair" the template. There is
# nothing to repair. Also note `"think": false` in a request is IGNORED by this
# model -- it reasons regardless.
FROM MiniMax-M2.7:Q3_K_S

PARAMETER stop "[e~["

# 65536 is well inside the native limit (config.json max_position_embeddings
# 204800; Ollama reports 196608), so no rope scaling is involved.
# KV cache at 62 layers / 8 KV heads / head_dim 128 is ~0.24 MiB per token:
# ~15.5 GiB here against ~9.7 GiB at the stock 40960. Use
# OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0 to halve it if this spills out of VRAM.
PARAMETER num_ctx 65536

# Vendor-recommended samplers, from the model card and generation_config.json.
# Ollama's own defaults (temp 0.8, top_p 0.9) are NOT these.
#
# Note that temperature here is inert for benchmark runs: ai_code_review.yml
# always sends AI_ASSISTANT_MODEL_TEMPERATURE (default 0.3), and a request
# option overrides the Modelfile. top_p/top_k ARE left blank by the workflow,
# so those two do take effect.
PARAMETER temperature 1.0
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 40

# The base tag carries a leftover SYSTEM block from the misdiagnosis phase:
#   "You must output your thoughts inside clear <think> and </think> tags ..."
# That instruction is at best redundant -- the model has a native thinking
# capability and Ollama parses reasoning into message.thinking -- and at worst
# it presses the model to emit the very "</think>" string that the old bad stop
# was truncating on. It also displaces MiniMax's own default system prompt.
#
# It cannot be blanked: SYSTEM """""" is IGNORED by ollama create and the
# inherited value survives (verified against a scratch model). Only a non-empty
# SYSTEM replaces it. So restore the model card's documented default here.
# Clearing it outright would require rebuilding from the GGUF.
#
# Note this only matters if the TEMPLATE references {{ .System }} -- see the
# pre-flight check above. A {{ .Prompt }} template drops SYSTEM silently.

# --- Standard SYSTEM prompt (fleet-wide) ----------------------------------
# Identical on every model in the benchmark, so the system prompt stops being an
# uncontrolled variable. Before this, the fleet ran a mix: "/no_think Be concise
# and skip chain-of-thought" on the six Qwen3.x builds, an expert-engineer
# persona on Qwen3-Coder-30B, a "detailed answers" persona on Qwen3.5-122B and
# Qwen3-32B, "Reasoning strength: high" on Muse-Glimmer-30B, and nothing at all
# on Gemma-4-31B -- none of it recorded in any scorecard.
#
# A non-empty SYSTEM replaces an inherited one, so this works whether the FROM
# line points at a blob or a tag. Keep it byte-identical across every model:
# the moment one differs, cross-model comparison is confounded again.
#
# Task instructions do NOT belong here -- they live in review_prompt.md, which
# is SHA-tracked in every scorecard. This line is persona only.
#
# This replaces two earlier attempts on this model: the vendor default
# ("Your name is MiniMax-M2.7..."), and a "Be exhaustive rather than brief"
# variant that drove a 45-minute run straight through the num_predict cap.
SYSTEM """You are an expert computer programmer with an eye for detail, who loves to provide high quality answers."""
